────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Third-party work
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

The speech synthesizer embedded in client.js is a derivative of bibibobo:

    bibibobo — https://github.com/hakihakii/bibibobo
    Copyright (c) 2026 hakihakii (Lumoswitch)
    Released under the MIT License

The embedded code is a verbatim copy of bibibobo.js with only the `export`
keywords removed, so that it can be bundled into a browser module. The audio
synthesis logic is unmodified.

Roles, kept separate because they are different things:

  * The sound itself comes from the scoring script of the Bilibili series
    《路墨小剧场》 by the channel 哈基科技
    (https://space.bilibili.com/3707062397700195). That is where these
    waveforms, formant pairs and voice scales originate.
  * The code that turns that sound into a reusable library is bibibobo.js,
    first committed by soraincloud (af11592, 2026-11-15).
  * hakihakii is the GitHub Organization that hosts the project; it is not
    an individual author account.
  * The playback approach used here — decoding to WAV and driving an `<audio>`
    element rather than an AudioContext, so that iOS Safari plays sound even in
    silent mode — follows upstream commit 3ac39a2 by KanbaraDYD.

